response:
 The internal angles of $\angle ADE$ must sum to 180 degrees, so $$\angle ADE = (180 - 70)/ 2 = 55^\circ$$ So, let $\beta = \angle DEC$ and $\alpha = \angle EBC$, then:  \begin{align*}
\beta &= 2 \cdot 55^\circ \\
\alpha + \beta &= 180^\circ \\[3mm]
\alpha &= 180^\circ - 2 \cdot 55^\circ \\
\alpha &= \boxed{70^\circ}
\end{align*} </think> <answer> 70^\circ </answer>

